[Music]  a farewell to another live car short the  mounting tool of this conflict now in  his third week  21 year old alexander velishko was  killed on the first day of the war  he was on the front line in the lugans  region in the east of the country  it took two weeks for his body to be  retrieved and brought back to his  hometown  i was in touch with him the day before  this happened his spirits were high it's  difficult to describe the loss hard to  express the army didn't change him he  was the same he was very kind perhaps  i'm being pathetic but he definitely  loved life  sounds ironic now  president vladimir zelinsky says about 1  300 servicemen have lost their lives so  far but key ukrainian cities remain  surrounded as russia seems to be  expanding its targets around the country  it might take longer because the  ukrainian army is actually putting up a  fight but it seems that the russian  strategy is to surround cities like  kharkiv in the northeast or maripo in  the south besiege them and bring them  down to their knees before continuing  the advance and people here are leaving  because they feel that dinipro could be  next  the nipro was targeted for two days  trades with rockets coming from the east  either from territory under separatist  control or russia itself  this was an early morning missile  intercepted over the city center that  was caught on mobile phone  our air defense system is weaker than at  the beginning of the war the russians  targeted it on the first day they tried  to destroy it  we managed to evacuate staff it's  working still but not everything is  smooth  now they fire aimlessly from a long  distance they don't come close because  we still have a defense system but they  have capacity to hit from hundreds of  kilometers away  we ask the whole of the world to close  the sky  while ukraine's western allies are  refusing to enforce a no-fly zone it's  the families who are left to live with  their loss  alexander had married valeria less than  three months ago  now she's a young widow holding tight  the colors her husband defended to his  last breath  hoping it won't be in vain  ukraine

